{{/*
The defects that break a claim by SUCCEEDING.

Three variants over one shape: a method that answers where the claim
says it must refuse. The context arms red because their primitives judge
a nil error, and a subject that ignores the context it is handed reports
none — which is the defect the claim is named for, not an accident of
the double.

The shape is a bare `return` under named results. That is what lets this
work for any signature: each slot yields its own zero without this file
naming a type it may not be able to spell, and no sample value has to be
invented for a result whose type nothing here can construct.
*/}}
{{- define "suite.defect.ctx-swap" -}}
{{ template "suite.frag.defect-answers" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "suite.defect.accepts-nil" -}}
{{ template "suite.frag.defect-answers" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "suite.frag.defect-answers" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				// The context arrives and is not read; the bare return
				// answers every slot's zero, which for the error slot is
				// the nil this claim forbids.
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /*
The idempotent claim's defect: the first call lands, the second refuses.

A closure over one bool rather than a counter — the claim is about the
repeat and nothing past it, and a counter would invite a reader to
wonder what the third call does.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.defect.second-call-errs" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		called := false
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				if called {
					{{ .ErrSlot }} = {{ renderExpr (external "errors" "New") }}({{ printf "%q" .RepeatMessage }})
					return
				}
				called = true
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /*
The substring the red must contain, appended where this generator can
quote the message from its declared home. Absent where the failure's
prose is authored in a body template, which has no constant to quote —
a weaker proof, said out loud rather than left to look identical.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.frag.defect-reason" -}}
{{- if .ReasonConst }}.Reasoned({{ renderExpr (external .Vocab .ReasonConst) }}){{ end }}
{{- end -}}
